From 0a2eb8797bf8e747bb28658b991295e92644bbda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:50:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): notice guarantee judges remote notices by
 their stored flag, stamps a failing row once [daveey]

A notice about a card on another gateway stores the OWNER's board name plus gateway=<owner>. The guarantee's
blocked_on_human opened that board locally: kanban_db_connect refused it ('kanban board bb does not exist'),
guarantee_pass logged and moved on without marking the row, and the same notice was retried every pass
(349 warnings in one window on the MacBook) while the chat never got a close-out or outcome refresh.

- kanban_remote_notices: both writers (sweep metadata, collect items) record blocked_on_human from the
  replicated task (status/block_kind/human_request); the open-chat poller copies it onto its persisted row.
- notice_guarantee.blocked_on_human: a notice with a foreign gateway, or only remote: event keys, returns that
  flag and never opens a local board; a local notice whose board is gone reads as not blocked.
- guarantee_pass: a candidate whose handling raises is stamped closeout.state=error (CAS) and refreshed, so it
  is handled once and left unresolved for the auditor instead of retried forever.

Self-heal defect kanban-a9b5d2c7c1.
